      en: "Nouakchott Modern Square is the primary public square in Mauritania's capital, built in the 1960s post-independence and renovated in the 2000s. It connects key government buildings and commercial areas. The square features a large fountain, palm trees, and benches. It is used for national celebrations, political rallies, and cultural festivals. Its design incorporates traditional Moorish arches and modern concrete structures, symbolizing Mauritania's blend of heritage and modernity.",
